    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0612" n="562" xml:id="pg562"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 160.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 184, of January, 1894 (day not given), and to approve your action in issuing
                    a passport to the minor, Joseph Wingfield, on the assumption that his American
                    birth and citizenship were established to your satisfaction. In the case of a
                    minor satisfactory proof of intent to return to the United States before or on
                    obtaining majority may be accepted, even though the intended sojourn abroad may
                    exceed two years.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
